x86_64-linux  a static local in cxx1's own spelling (`f.n`, `.guard`) where clang writes `_ZZ`/`_ZGVZ` or `?n@?1??f@@` and `?$TSS` - docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "A static local keeps its own name in the object file", as static-local-dynamic-init.nonames records; the complete-object constructor or destructor of an inline special member, which clang on ELF folds into C2/D2 (-mconstructor-aliases) - emission, not a name (classed by r6d, 2026-11-15).
x86_64-windows  a static local in cxx1's own spelling (`f.n`, `.guard`) where clang writes `_ZZ`/`_ZGVZ` or `?n@?1??f@@` and `?$TSS` - docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "A static local keeps its own name in the object file", as static-local-dynamic-init.nonames records (classed by r6d, 2026-11-15).
